<h2 class="doc-h2">SidebarGroup</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    A labelled section. <code>SidebarGroupAction</code> is the button that belongs to the group
    rather than to a row in it — "add a project", not "act on this project".
</p>
<Example Source="SidebarGroupExample.razor"><SidebarGroupExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Collapsible group</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    shadcn wraps the group in a <code>Collapsible</code> and makes the label its trigger. The
    collapsible here IS a <code>&lt;details&gt;</code>, so the fold is the browser's: it works with
    no script, it is in the page for a crawler, and the chevron turns on <code>[open]</code>.
</p>
<Example Source="SidebarGroupCollapsible.razor"><SidebarGroupCollapsible /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">SidebarMenuButton</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    <code>Active</code> is the current page, and with <code>[up-nav]</code> on the menu you rarely
    set it: Unpoly compares each href with the address bar and marks the match, which keeps working
    after a fragment swap because the swap is what changed the address bar.
</p>
<Example Source="SidebarMenuButtonExample.razor"><SidebarMenuButtonExample /></Example>

